ClientSort uses code from:
- Mouse Wheelie by Siphalor (Apache-2.0): item comparison, client-side sorting.
- Inventory Management by Roundaround (MIT): trigger buttons and their layout.

The button sprites in mixins/clientsort/runtime.rs (module `sprites`) are
ClientSort's own textures (assets/clientsort/textures/gui/sprites/widget),
converted to rows of pixels. The icon in mixins/clientsort/data/icon.png is
ClientSort's catalog icon.

The config screen (mixins/clientsort/cloth.rs) follows Cloth Config by
shedaniel (https://github.com/shedaniel/cloth-config, LGPL-3.0), rewritten in
Rust; its sprites in mixins/clientsort/cloth_sprites.rs are Cloth Config's
texture (assets/cloth-config2/textures/gui/cloth_config.png), converted to
rows of pixels, and its texts are Cloth Config's and ClientSort's own.

This port rewrites ClientSort's logic in Rust for Horizon's native mod API.
It is not affiliated with TerminalMC, Mojang or Microsoft.
